## Abstract

This update is based on direct inspection of the repository `seating_arrangement_optimizer_final`, not on a generic event-planning template. The implemented system is a repository-local full-stack application composed of: (1) an Expo/React Native client in `ui/`, (2) a Flask-based asynchronous solver service in `solver/`, (3) an nginx reverse proxy and static page, and (4) direct Firebase SDK usage for authentication and Firestore persistence. The only server-side API exposed by the repository is the seating solver; event, group, guest, and arrangement CRUD are managed client-side in React context and then synchronized to Firestore. The optimization core models social structure as a weighted guest tree and applies NSGA-II with heuristic initializers and optional GNN-seeded initialization. The repository also contains substantial research and report-generation code (`run_all.py`, `train_and_evaluate_gnn.py`, `report.tex`, figures, tuning outputs), but these files are not on the normal web runtime path. Where the repository does not provide evidence for a capability, this document states that explicitly rather than inferring it.

