## 4. User Stories

The following user stories are grounded in implemented screens, store actions, and solver behavior found in the repository.

1. As an event planner, I can create a new event with a name and optional date.
2. As an event planner, I can clone an existing event's guest tree into a new event as a starting point.
3. As an event planner, I can build a hierarchy of guest groups with multiple roots, nested subgroups, and direct guests.
4. As an event planner, I can set a group distance weight and re-parent or reorder groups without creating cycles in the tree.
5. As an event planner, I can add guest details such as phone, email, notes, expected attendance, and gift description.
6. As an event planner, I can search guests within an event by name, phone, or email.
7. As an event planner, I can generate seating candidates by configuring max table size, `alpha`, `p`, and optional depth weighting.
8. As an event planner, I can review generated candidates and explicitly save only the arrangements I want to keep.
9. As an event planner, I can open a saved arrangement, search for a guest by name, and move guests between tables with undo/redo support.
10. As an event planner, I can inspect a saved arrangement either as tables or as a color-coded tree map.
11. As an event planner, I can focus on one subtree and see only the tables that contain guests from that subtree, while still seeing outside guests dimmed for context.
12. As an event planner, I can export a subtree from one event into another event.
13. As a user, I can continue without account on web, or sign in with Google so my event data is written to Firestore.
14. As a user, I can open a static explanatory page (`/about.html`) and, in debug mode, preload a large demo event generated by the solver support scripts.

