## 9. Conclusion

The repository implements a concrete and internally coherent architecture, but it is narrower and more specific than the original draft implied. The real system consists of a client-heavy Expo application with direct Firebase persistence, a dedicated Flask optimization service for seating generation, nginx-based web delivery, and a separate research track for tuning and GNN training. The architecture is strongest when documented as a hybrid application plus research repository, not as a conventional CRUD backend with solver add-ons.

This updated document preserves the original report structure while correcting the main inaccuracies: the absence of event-management REST APIs, the direct Firestore data path, the transient nature of generated candidates, the web-only Docker startup path, the optional rather than guaranteed runtime role of the GNN, and the difference between production code and research/report artifacts.
